(1) Problem Statement

SkillsTrack Training Centre currently records learner goals, tasks, support bookings and progress across separate documents and messages. This makes it difficult for learners to stay organised and track their learning progress. Assessors also struggle to identify outstanding work, monitor learner performance and provide timely support. The organisation requires a browser-based Learner Support Portal that centralises task management, support bookings, progress tracking, learning resources and learner engagement features. 

(2) The two user typies 

(2.1) User 1: Learner 
Responsibilities: 

Register an account 
Sign in and sign out 
Manage own tasks 

In Scope 
The system will include: 

User registration 
Login and logout 
Task management (Create, Read, Update, Delete) 
Progress dashboard 
Support session booking 
Learning resources section 
Search and filter functionality 
Coding mini-game 
Printable progress report 
Firebase database storage
User authentication 
View learning progress 
Access learning resources 
Play the coding mini-game 
Print progress summary 

(2.2) User 2: Assessor/Administrator 

Responsibilities: 
View support bookings 
Monitor learner activity 
Monitor learner progress 
Update support booking status 

In Scope 
The system will include: 

User registration 
Login and logout 
Task management (Create, Read, Update, Delete) 
Progress dashboard 
Support session booking 
Learning resources section 
Search and filter functionality 
Coding mini-game 
Printable progress report 
Firebase database storage 
User authentication 

Out of Scope 
The system will NOT include: 

Online payments 
Video conferencing 
SMS notifications 
Attendance tracking 
Course creation tools 
Financial management 
Mobile app development 
AI tutoring system 

(3) List Project Constraints

Constraints:

Must use JavaScript (ES6+) for application logic.
Must use Firebase Realtime Database.
Must use Firebase Authentication.
Must be browser-based.
Must use GitHub for version control.
Must be completed within two months.
Passwords cannot be stored in cookies or the database directly.
Firebase security rules must restrict unauthorised access

